# The brain's schedule. Times are local to the container, which takes TZ from
# .env — set it, or the night shift and the morning plan land in the wrong
# part of someone else's day.
#
# Both scripts write their own logs (brain/.morning.log, brain/.night.log) and
# both refuse to run twice in a day, so a container restart cannot double up.
# The night shift additionally does nothing at all until night.enabled is set
# in brain/config.json.

# The morning plan, before anyone is up.
0 7 * * * cd /brain && bash brain/tools/morning.sh

# The heavy jobs, in their own usage window, five hours clear of the morning.
0 1 * * * cd /brain && bash brain/tools/night.sh
